/* Three Kingdoms Daily: shared officer database.
   Every game loads this file, so a name added here is recognised everywhere.

   One entry per person:
     n    name shown in the games          a    other spellings players can type
     zh   Chinese name                      cn   courtesy name
     f    faction (Wei, Shu, Wu, Jin, Other) g    gender (M or F)
     r    role (Ruler, General, Strategist, Official, Consort)
     b,d  birth and death years (bc/dc = 1 means approximate)
     h    home province (the Han province of their home commandery, around 190)
     home ancestral home as the source writes it
     side allegiance as the source gives it
     k    H historical, N appears only in the novel, F later folklore or games, G only in Koei's RTK games
     src  where the facts come from (record volume or novel note)
     u    index into URLS, the page the facts were taken from
     dn   note on a date
     mo   position in the Mystery Officer answer list (keeps every daily puzzle unchanged)

   Main sources: Wikipedia's "List of people of the Three Kingdoms" (A to Z), which cites
   the Sanguozhi (Records of the Three Kingdoms), Houhanshu and Jin Shu; Wikipedia's
   "List of fictional people of the Three Kingdoms" for novel only characters; individual
   Wikipedia articles where a person is not on the lists; Kongming's Archives RTK8 roster
   for the five officers no other source covers. Built October 2026. */
